Jupiter ascending is not a bad film it's  merely a ridiculously flawed film I love  this movie flaws and all for me it's in  the same sphere as Chronicles of Riddick  a offbeat space opera that is a thing  that should not exist but it does and  the world is all the better for it in  fact it's not just in the same sphere as  Chronicles of Riddick I love it for many  of the same reasons aesthetically  they're similar building on the  tradition of dune with a universe that  is filled with a society that is ancient  and bloated and cracking at the seams  they both draw on art deco and baroque  as a visual shorthand for opulence and  corruption and age Titus has nude heroic  statues lining the docking bay of his  capital ship the Necromongers fly around  in an oversized Oscar statuette so I was  rewatching Jupiter ascending when this  notion came up in my Twitter feed is  Jupiter Jones an empowered character  it's an interesting question because it  requires us to turn the lens not merely  on the film itself but the underlying  assumption of what is it that makes a  character empowered an empowered  character is a character that has plot  agency often as a shorthand we'll look  at how a character moves through the  plot both literally and metaphorically  are they a character who goes places or  are they a character who is brought  places most of the time that works well  enough because a character who is varied  from scene to scene is usually a  character without a lot of will or  agency but that shorthand is I feel  insufficient in this case and so we need  to look instead at composure while  Jupiter is often very very often set on  the back foot by other characters  looking to manipulate her for their own  ends she has never made the fool by  these manipulations rather than being  pushed around by the plot the plot is  explicitly about Jupiter competing in an  environment where the main weapon is  information and she is fighting at a  disadvantage the fact that she's a quick  study and is able to often hold her  weight when the odds are stacked against  her is a running theme of the film that  injects her with an agency that is  otherwise bolide by the fact that she is  so often carried from place to place  while unconscious this is a nuanced  distinct  the difference between a character that  is lacking in plot agency and a  character that is deceived and  manipulated by other characters this in  my opinion leans towards the latter the  plot is mired in politics with power  players maneuvering against one another  trying to use Jupiter and other  characters as pawns in their corporate  schemes the main characters being  tricked deceived cheated betrayed these  are core elements of conflict in this  kind of story while she is being  constantly told where to go and what to  do she frequently challenges these  assertions and tries to exert her own  will she comes up with her own plans and  maneuvers and pushes for others to yield  to her instead when she does accept  things without question it's an  expression of trust building further on  the interpersonal conflicts at the core  of the story as a result when her agency  is subverted or denied it is usually at  the diegetic level a result of conflict  a result of other characters trying to  manipulate her rather than being a story  convenience for the writers and this is  why composure is the important element  as written and acted how does Jupiter  hold herself and how is she then framed  by the camera the music and the editing  despite the fact that Jupiter is so  often literally carried from place to  place the movie doesn't treat her as a  thing even as other characters do  Jupiter retains plot agency even as the  plot revolves around other characters  trying to subvert her personal agency  there's an organic conflict to it a  back-and-forth of Parry and riposte that  drives things forward  is she sometimes powerless are her plans  sometimes deeply flawed does she get  duped into making terrible choices well  of course it's a story and that's how  our stories work but even then in those  moments her decisions still drive the  plot because a character being empowered  is not about them getting their way it's  about them influencing where the story  goes so go in peace my children in the  name of like share and subscribe amen
 

